  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Negate the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ For all $r\\in Q,$ $r\\ne \\frac{1}{2}.$",
  "worked_solution": "If we denote\n\n$$\nP(r):r=\\frac{1}{2},\n$$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n\u2200r\\in Q,\\,\u00acP(r).\n$$\n\nNegating this, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u00ac(\u2200r\\in Q,\\,\u00acP(r)) & \u2261\u2203r\\in Q,\\,\u00ac\u00acP(r) \\\\  & \u2261\u2203r\\in Q,\\,P(r).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $\u2203r\\in Q,\\,P(r)$ reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **There exists** $r\\in Q$ such that $r=\\frac{1}{2}.$",
